def _msToFolder(ms):
    """The day folder a thumbnail for `ms` belongs in -- LOCAL date.

    Local, not UTC: a thumbnail is filed under the day the operator saw the
    event, so an evening event does not appear under tomorrow's date.  Changed
    2026-09-06 at the owner's request.

    This MATCHES the clip day folder, which has always been local.  Clips are
    filed by StreamReader._registerRemuxSegment, which slices the date out of
    the segment filename ffmpeg's `-f segment` muxer wrote with LOCAL strftime
    -- no timezone conversion in Python at all.  Verified over 4,000 clipdb
    rows: of the 727 whose local and UTC dates differ, 727 are under the local
    name and none under UTC.

    So this change did not separate thumbnails from their clips, it reunited
    them: thumbnails were the only thing here filed by UTC, which put an
    evening thumbnail one day ahead of the clip it belongs to.

    (StreamReader._roll_clip DOES build a UTC folder name, but that is the
    re-encode fallback, not the live stream-copy path.  Reading it as the live
    path is what produced the wrong conclusion this comment used to carry.)

    Three functions must agree on this and are changed together:
    this one writes the thumbnail, DataManager._msToFolder finds it, and
    DiskCleaner._enumDateFolders deletes it.
    """
    return datetime.fromtimestamp(ms / 1000.0).strftime('%Y-%m-%d')

